<title>HUNGARY: Hungary govt approves cut in monthly devaluation.</title>
<headline>Hungary govt approves cut in monthly devaluation.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's crawling devaluation will be reduced to one percent monthly from the current 1.1 percent, from August 15, a government spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The crawling peg devaluation will be one percent from the middle of August, compared with the present 1.1 percent,&quot; government spokesman Elemer Kiss told a news conference following a weekly government meeting.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
